    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d799">

                <pb facs="0791" n="779" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.00 Statement July 16, 1937/174:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Istanbul</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-11T18:00:00+02:00">August 11, 1937—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Reference your telegram No. 63, August 5, 6 p.m.<anchor n="20"
                        xml:id="d799-f1"/> The Foreign Minister says that he is much touched by your
                    message and like you is gratified to note similarity which exists between the
                    policies of the United States and Turkey.</p>
                <p>He asked whether he may give your message to the press.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d799-f1" n="20" xml:id="d799-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram No. 36, August 5, 6 p.m., to the Chargé in Iran, <ref
                        target="#pg753">p. 753</ref>.</p>
            </note>
